omap_dma: raise END_FRAME for unsynchronised transfers too

The end-of-frame interrupt (CICR FRAME_IE) fires at the end of every frame;
QEMU only raised it for frame-synchronised transfers (sync && fs). Linux's
omap-dma engine does memcpy as one unsynchronised frame with FRAME_IE as the
completion interrupt, so every such transfer finished silently. On the N810
6.18's omap2-onenand driver waited out each one ("timeout waiting for DMA")
and fell back to PIO.

diff --git a/hw/dma/omap_dma.c b/hw/dma/omap_dma.c
index 77797a67b..9b1ea8c01 100644
--- a/hw/dma/omap_dma.c
+++ b/hw/dma/omap_dma.c
@@ -558,7 +558,7 @@ static void omap_dma_transfer_setup(struct soc_dma_ch_s *dma)
                     (a->element >= (a->elements >> 1) ? a->elements : 0) -
                     a->element)
     INTR_CHECK(
-                    ch->sync && ch->fs && (ch->interrupts & END_FRAME_INTR),
+                    ch->interrupts & END_FRAME_INTR,
                     omap_dma_intr_frame,
                     a->elements - a->element)
     INTR_CHECK(
